  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 131 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThe pattern trends drier during the latter half of the week as \nridging strengthens over Texas. The hot and very un-autumn-like \nweather is expected to continue through the weekend, with highs in \nthe 90s and lows still largely in the 70s. One wrinkle in the \nforecast is that the high amplitude ridging will allow drier air to \nbe siphoned off from the Midwest, which will allow dew points to \ndrop into the 50s Friday and possibly Saturday mainly north of \nInterstate 10, providing more of a dry heat. This will be short-\nlived as southerly flow restrengthens ahead of a trough over the \nwestern US, resulting in a return to more humid conditions to start \nnext week.\n\nRain chances stay low Wednesday into the weekend, limited to the \nsmall potential for a brief shower closer to the coast or to the Rio \nGrande. Heading into next week, a subtropical jet streak bolstered \nby western troughing is forecast to squash the ridge southward, and \nthis is reflected across both the medium range deterministic and \nensemble guidance. This favors a possible shift towards a more \nactive weather pattern next week to close out September and usher in \nOctober.",
